# REQUIRED COMPANION FILE

Create `scripts/validate-readonly-query.sh` at the project root (or wherever your hook path points):

```bash
#!/bin/bash
# Block SQL write operations; allow SELECT queries.

INPUT=$(cat)
COMMAND=$(echo "$INPUT" | jq -r '.tool_input.command // empty')

if [ -z "$COMMAND" ]; then
  exit 0
fi

# Block write operations (case-insensitive, word-boundary match)
if echo "$COMMAND" | grep -iE '\b(INSERT|UPDATE|DELETE|DROP|CREATE|ALTER|TRUNCATE|REPLACE|MERGE|GRANT|REVOKE)\b' > /dev/null; then
  echo "Blocked: Write operations not allowed. Use SELECT queries only." >&2
  exit 2
fi

# Block stored procedure execution (may contain writes)
if echo "$COMMAND" | grep -iE '\b(CALL|EXEC|EXECUTE)\b' > /dev/null; then
  echo "Blocked: Stored procedure execution not allowed (may contain writes)." >&2
  exit 2
fi

exit 0
```

Make it executable: `chmod +x ./scripts/validate-readonly-query.sh`

On Windows, write the equivalent in PowerShell and add `shell: powershell` to the hook entry.

## Adapting this template

To restrict to a different operation set (e.g., "allow only specific CLI tools"):
1. Change the `description` to match the new restriction
2. Rewrite the validation script's grep patterns
3. Update "What you can do" / "What you cannot do" in the body to match
